          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora classifies the source files stored in a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "partials"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " directory as partial files, or partials for short. Partials are usually AsciiDoc files that contain content snippets, such as common descriptions or terminology, that are inserted into one or more pages or partials. However, Antora doesn’t require partials to be AsciiDoc files."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page$partials.adoc"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "metadata": {
                  "role": "bare include"
                },
                "target": "page:page$partials.adoc"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A partial isn’t required to have a file extension. Unlike a publishable resource that’s treated as a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "hidden file"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "standard-directories.html#hidden-files"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " if it’s missing a file extension, Antora will load a partial that doesn’t have a file extension into its content catalog and assign the partial a resource ID for referencing."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora doesn’t publish partial files as individual site pages. A "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "partial must be referenced by an include directive"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "page:include-a-partial.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " from a page, or resource that’s eventually included in a page, for the partial’s content to be published."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Except when it’s typical for a file type to not have a file extension, it’s a good practice to save your partial source files with their valid file extensions."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "important"
          }
        ],
